# Copy this file to .env (same folder as vite.config.js) if you want to
# turn on the optional CAPTCHA widget. Nothing here is required — the
# app builds and runs fully with zero config; the CAPTCHA widget simply
# doesn't render, and the corresponding backend check no-ops too (see
# backend/.env.example's RECAPTCHA_SECRET_KEY).
#
# IMPORTANT: Vite only exposes env vars prefixed VITE_ to frontend code
# (anything else is silently invisible to import.meta.env, by design —
# it's how Vite keeps non-VITE_ backend secrets out of the browser
# bundle). The file must be named exactly `.env` and live here in
# frontend/ (next to vite.config.js). Restart `npm run dev` after
# editing it — Vite only reads env vars at server startup.

# The SAME site's key from google.com/recaptcha/admin that you used for
# RECAPTCHA_SECRET_KEY in backend/.env — this is the public "site key"
# half of that pair (safe to expose in frontend code; it identifies
# which site is asking, not a secret). See frontend/src/components/Captcha.jsx.
# VITE_RECAPTCHA_SITE_KEY=
